eartbeat tick and received MsgHeartbeat',['s-heartbeat','s-follower','s-step'],consumes_fact_ids=['f-commit'],produces_fact_ids=['f-commit'],implementation_guards=['Sender caps Commit at min(peer Match,local committed). Receiver Step filters terms.'],writes=['Follower commitTo is monotone and checks lastIndex.'],external_effects=['Return heartbeat response, which does not constitute append-index support.'])\nprofile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go raft library. Node serializes raft execution in its run goroutine; RawNode requires caller serialization. Transport, disk durability and application/client completion are caller duties; in-repository MemoryStorage and configuration recovery remain implementation support, not externalized unknown code.',protocol_contexts=['Node identity, term/role, log entry term/index, active incoming/outgoing voters, read request context'],external_interfaces=['Node/RawNode Propose, Step, Tick, Ready, Advance, ApplyConfChange','Storage.InitialState/Entries/Term/Snapshot'],ownership=['raft owns protocol state; caller owns persistent writes, transport and application'],variants=['Synchronous Ready/Advance','AsyncStorageWrites with ordered local append/apply workers','PreVote, CheckQuorum, joint consensus, learners, StepDownOnRemoval'],source_ids=['s-api','s-node-loop','s-ready-contract','s-storage-interface','s-init'])\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivities=[]\nfor a,role in roles.items():\n activities.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=role['relation'],realization_summary={'A1':'Append support is aggregated under active voters and current-term log matching; leader propagates committed prefix.','A2':'Election votes acquire local authority; term, role, lease and quorum checks limit its use.','A3':'Stored log and ConfState reconstruct participation; snapshots resynchronize lagging nodes.','A4':'Application activates configuration entries; Changer maintains joint/learner eligibility.','A5':'Ready or ordered apply messages export committed entries with separate completion bookkeeping.','A6':'Unstable overlay, caller persistence and deferred responses mediate support publication.','A7':'Proposal submission is distinct from committed entry/application completion; ReadIndex uses caller context.'}[a],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for b in B if b['primary_activity']==a for s in b['source_ids']))))\noverview=dict(status='usable',rationale='The representative proposal, vote/term transition and old-work paths have been followed through actual quorum, log, storage-message and membership callees. This is a source-grounded backbone for selecting questions, not a correctness judgment or exhaustive coverage.',formation=dict(explanation='A serialized RawNode.Propose (or node.run proposal event) enters raft.Step. A follower forwards to a known leader or drops; a candidate drops. A leader rejects transfer/removal/quota cases, assigns term/index, appends locally and broadcasts predecessor-qualified MsgApp. Followers check predecessor and committed-prefix conflicts, append only conflicting suffixes, bound advertised commit, and queue replies. Both follower replies and leader self-acks pass through msgsAfterAppend; legal publication relies on caller persistence, directly via Ready/Advance or ordered async append Responses. The leader term-filters replies and raises sender Match. Tracker considers only active voters, majority order statistics and both halves of joint configuration. raftLog.maybeCommit additionally requires the candidate entry to match the current term. Commit propagates via append or Match-capped heartbeat. Ready exports committed entries; async apply waits for local stability. Application and public client completion remain separate caller actions; proposal acceptance does not promise commitment.',behavior_ids=['b-entry','b-proposal','b-follower-append','b-send-durable','b-aggregate','b-heartbeat','b-apply'],fact_ids=['f-entry','f-append-response','f-commit'],source_ids=['s-api','s-role','s-follower','s-send','s-ready-storage','s-ack','s-tracker','s-joint','s-majority','s-log-eligibility','s-heartbeat','s-log-apply','s-guide']),context=dict(explanation='Ticks or Campaign trigger hup only when promotable and without unapplied committed configuration changes. PreVote can gather prospective support without increasing term; real candidacy resets state, increments term and records self vote. Self and remote vote replies are queued behind persistence. Vote grants require vote/leader eligibility and last-log freshness. Matching response type and active voter quorum determine victory; the new leader resets progress and appends its current-term empty entry. Higher-term messages normally force follower transition, with lease/pre-vote exceptions; obsolete responses are rejected. CheckQuorum can cause same-term stepdown. Transfer pauses proposals, catches the target up and sends TimeoutNow; timeout or ineligibility aborts transfer. Restart restores HardState/log/configuration and starts as follower. Configuration entries activate through ApplyConfChange, changing voters and optionally causing removal stepdown.',behavior_ids=['b-election','b-context-reset','b-config','b-recover'],fact_ids=['f-vote','f-leader','f-config'],source_ids=['s-role','s-step','s-follower','s-vote-count','s-log-eligibility','s-transfer-read','s-recovery-config','s-init','s-config']),connection=dict(explanation='Term/role reset clears election tally, remote replication support and readOnly acknowledgments, while preserving log and committed prefix; current-term matching prevents a fresh leader from advancing commitment solely using an old-term candidate index. Queued/in-flight responses may outlive resets, so Step term checks remain necessary. StorageAppendResp carries both creation term and entry identity: old-term entry stabilization is skipped even if entry term/index recur, but committed snapshot application survives that term change. StorageApplyResp is term-zero and represents committed work independent of leadership. Configuration changes retain existing participant progress but change which IDs count; switching configuration can immediately rerun commitment. Snapshots recover configuration as well as log boundary. Safe reads wait for current-term commitment (except singleton shortcut), track context-specific heartbeat acknowledgments under active voters, then expose read index to a caller that still must wait for application. reset replaces readOnly but does not clear pendingReadIndexMessages; release retries them only after a current-term commit, creating fresh acknowledgment tracking.',behavior_ids=['b-context-reset','b-send-durable','b-aggregate','b-config','b-recover','b-apply'],fact_ids=['f-commit','f-config','f-leader'],source_ids=['s-role','s-step','s-ready-storage','s-unstable','s-recovery-config','s-read-context','s-read-release','s-read-contract','s-transfer-read','s-leader-entry']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Resolve doc.go same-batch persistence concurrency versus Ready.Messages entries-before-send interface before testing that weaker schedule.','Read-only lease assumptions, retry context reuse and survival of pending reads across multiple terms need focused applicability review.','MemoryStorage compaction/error paths, detailed bootstrap and all flow-control failure variants are not exhaustively mapped.','An internal Advance/applied update is not proof that external application or client return completed.'])\nsurfaces=[dict(entry_point='doc.go usage step 2 versus node.go Ready.Messages',disposition='deferred',reason='The package usage text permits messages while same-batch entries persist; Ready requires sending after Entries persist. This is a concrete contract ambiguity affecting the legality of a delayed-storage schedule, not an established violation.',source_ids=['s-guide','s-ready-contract','s-send'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='raft.reset / releasePendingReadIndexMessages / readOnly.addRequest',disposition='deferred',reason='Pending pre-commit reads survive reset while heartbeat acknowledgment state is replaced. Fresh current-term release is a protection; precise retry/context and invocation responsibility remain to be investigated.',source_ids=['s-role','s-read-release','s-read-context','s-read-contract'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Storage implementation and application worker',disposition='externalized',reason='Disk persistence and externally visible application/client effects are application duties. In-repository MemoryStorage is support and is not evidence of disk durability.',source_ids=['s-storage-interface','s-guide','s-async-contract'])]\nPath('audit-map.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(version=1,target_profile=profile,activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=surfaces,core_overview=overview),indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nsub=dict(action='research',rationale='Register the initial source-grounded explanation of both core relationships and their connection before selecting a focused Candidate.',sources=sources,map_path='audit-map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['s-send','s-role','s-step','s-ready-contract','s-guide','s-tracker','s-recovery-config'],answered='Traced proposal entry through durable-response routing, voter-qualified aggregation, current-term commitment and application export; traced election, authority loss and storage/application work surviving transitions. No execution or correctness conclusion is claimed.',remaining=['Determine which synchronous persistence ordering contract is applicable to a concrete public API history.','Select a principal Fact lifecycle after resolving that legal-schedule premise; read-only pending context lifetime is an alternative frontier.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Next compare the precise Ready ordering statements and response production tests. This changes whether a deferred same-batch persistence schedule is a legal discriminator, avoiding an invented failure premise.'))\nPath('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_submission.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
